======================
The "baseline" AI type
======================

This directory is a frozen, vendored copy of the stock AI:

  ai/default/  -> ai/baseline/default/   (verbatim)
  ai/classic/  -> ai/baseline/classic/   (classicai.c, classicai.h verbatim)

taken at commit

  0896b34136bf96676926bab67ddfee68bdd964f2   (master, 2026-07-23)

and registered as the AI type "baseline"
(build with -Daimodules=classic,tex,baseline).

Why it exists
-------------

It is the measurement control for the deep-AI project
(doc/deep-ai/00-context.md). All benchmark comparisons are paired runs
against this snapshot. If it ever changes, every previously recorded
benchmark number becomes incomparable, so it must never change - even
if ai/default moves on after a rebase, and even to fix bugs.

It also lets old-style and new-style AIs play in the same game:

  create Foo baseline
  create Bar classic

both work, and both survive save/load (the per-player AI type is
persisted in savegames).

How the no-collision trick works
--------------------------------

The vendored sources are byte-identical to the snapshot commit. To let
them link into the same binary as the live ai/default and ai/classic,
the build force-includes ai/baseline/baseline_syms.h (see the
fc_ai_baseline static_library in meson.build), which #defines every
global symbol the vendored objects define to a bl_-prefixed name. The
list was generated with `nm --defined-only -g` over the compiled
ai/default and ai/classic objects at the snapshot commit.

The only new code is baselineai.c, a shim that calls the (renamed)
vendored fc_ai_classic_setup() and then renames the module to
"baseline". It also replaces the four savegame hooks
(player_save/load_relations, city_save/load) with wrappers using a
"baseline" savefile prefix: the vendored classic wrappers hardcode the
"ai" prefix, which the live classic module already writes, and every
registered module's save hook runs for every player, so sharing the
prefix produces duplicate savefile keys and an unloadable save.

Freeze enforcement
------------------

MANIFEST.sha256 records the hash of every file in this directory.
scripts/check-baseline-frozen.sh verifies it and is wired up as the
meson test "baseline-frozen". Do not regenerate the manifest; a
mismatch means the snapshot was modified and the change must be
reverted.
